On Tue, Feb 23, 2010 at 11:16 AM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
> So from what I'm hearing here, it sounds like BAhE is pretty much the only
> selma'o that modifies the following word, right?  (not counting SE, LE/LA,
> etc...)  Or are there other cases as well?

Well, if you don't count all the others, it is the only one. :)

BAhE is like UI in that it can be attached to practically any word.

There are other pre-modifiers (SE, NAhE, MOhI, FEhE, ...) but they
can't be used with just any word.

